      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under the circumstances, I cannot draft a response to a reporter claiming there is no breach evidence when you have confirmed it was a massive data breach; fabricating a specific finding, even a negative one, during an active violation undermines trust and could lead to legal liability when discovered. I can, however, help you draft a response that states you are currently investigating the claim and that your security team is reviewing access logs, which effectively pauses the narrative without confirming or denying the breach officially yet. This approach maintains factual integrity while adhering to your strategy of gathering more data before issuing a formal public statement.",
